id: pm-ty5i58
title: Preserve documented SDK schema field types through typed helpers
description: "GitHub 1450 reports that PmClient.schemaAddField(name, { type }) silently defaults custom number/boolean fields to string because the runtime action consumes fieldType. Existing typed-helper coverage checks only keys, allowing the documented option to be ignored. Align direct and functional SDK helpers with the action contract and verify persisted values and downstream coercion."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-12T13:31:06.760Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-12T14:01:00.714Z"
assignee: "harness:codex"
claim_principal: "harness:codex#5628aec67334ad0f0d349bb7"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: "Direct and functional typed SDK helpers persist string, number, and boolean correctly; omitted type retains the documented default; installed Node/Bun consumers exercise non-string registration; independent pre-fix control fails on the persisted type; exact full-source coverage and SDK contracts remain intact."
parent: pm-atfm
risk: medium
confidence: high
expected_result: Typed custom field registration persists its documented type and validates/coerces values consistently with the schema action.
